Test 1 - Email without @ symbol:
Command: curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/register.php -d 'username=invalidemail1&password=test123&email=notanemail'
Response: HTTP 200 OK - {"success":true,"message":"Registration successful."}

Test 2 - Email with @ but no domain:
Command: curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/register.php -d 'username=invalidemail2&password=test123&email=@nodomain'
Response: HTTP 200 OK - {"success":true,"message":"Registration successful."}

Test 3 - Empty email:
Command: curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/register.php -d 'username=emptyemail&password=test123&email='
Response: HTTP 200 OK - {"success":true,"message":"Registration successful."}

All invalid email formats are accepted without any validation errors or rejection messages.
